irly rigid protuberance or needlelike structure on an animal, shell, mushroom or plant. The botanical term technically refers to such a structure derived from a leaf or part of a leaf.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The male, as Dr. Gunther informs me, has a cluster of stiff, straight spines, like those of a comb, on the sides of the tail.", "reference": "1871, Charles Darwin, “chapter 12”, in Descent of Man, page 331:"}], "synonyms": ["needle", "prickle", "quill", "spicule", "spike", "thorn", "virgula"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(botany) The heartwood of trees.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(neuroscience) Ellipsis of dendritic spine.", "tags": ["abbreviation", "alt of", "ellipsis"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Spines are distinguished by the presence of globular tips called spine heads; when spines are present, the synapses innervating dendrites are made from these heads.", "reference": "2008, Dale Purves, George J. Augustine, David Fitzpatrick, William C. Hall, Anthony-Samuel LaMantia, James O. McNamara, Leonard E. White, Neuroscience, 4th edition, Sinauer Associates:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A linear payscale operated by some large organizations that allows flexibility for local and specific conditions.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["pay spine"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(geology) A tall mass of viscous lava extruded from a volcano.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "The stiffness of an arrow.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A central part which supports a whole; core.